Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Model Response and Interventional Effects for Species Distribution
    Models
Version: 0.11.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Audits model-based environmental responses in species
    distribution modelling. Predictor shifts evaluated over a fitted model
    produce effect sizes, dose-response curves and spatial maps. Variable selection is a two-stage screen whose second stage ranks
    predictors by the change they cause in the fitted probability when they
    are shifted while every other predictor is held at its observed value - a
    g-computation contrast - calibrated against a response-permutation null.
    The permutation importance of the same forest is reported alongside as a
    diagnostic; both permutation and additive shifts can leave joint data
    support. Effect products carry a range diagnostic: the fraction of evaluated
    rows inside the training quantile box before and after shifting. This does
    not establish conditional positivity or causal identification. Both
    sit in a complete workflow - Random Forest, BRT, MaxEnt and GAM learners,
    nested spatial cross-validation, ensemble prediction, and future climate
    projection with extrapolation control. The package targets interpretable
    interventional attribution under stated assumptions. Optional invariant
    selection uses 'tramicp' with supplied environment groups; its assumptions
    are not verified by the software. Scenario contrasts for GAMs can use
    'marginaleffects'. Outputs do not establish ecological causality or convert
    presence-background suitability to occurrence probability.
